/**
@mainpage ncr_picking Developer Reference

@section mp_overview Project Snapshot

`ncr_picking` is a Qt/C++ industrial vision-picking application, centered on `vc::model::ITask` /
`vc::model::TaskLocalization`.

It ships as **two peer executables**, not one application with a mode switch:

| Executable | Source | Audience |
|---|---|---|
| `ncr_picking.exe` | `components/app/` | Commissioning &mdash; build the project, configure devices, calibrate, teach patterns |
| `ncr_runtime.exe` | `runtime_app/` | Operator runtime &mdash; load a commissioned project and run it |

Neither shell may include the other. Both link the same `ncr_shared` static library built from
`src/`, and each can hand off to the other (see `vc::ui::presentShellWindow`).

Device integrations:
- Basler GigE camera (`vc::device::CameraBaslerGige`)
- JAI GigE camera over the Pleora eBUS SDK (`vc::device::JaiGigECamera`)
- Mitsubishi MC PLC (`vc::device::McProtocolDevice`) &mdash; 3E binary over Ethernet, 1C and 3C
  ASCII computer link over serial; see `docs/domains/mc_protocol/mc_protocol.md`
- Modbus TCP, both roles (`vc::device::ModbusTcpClientDevice` as master,
  `vc::device::ModbusTcpServerDevice` as slave). The server also implements
  `vc::device::IResultOutputDevice`, so **one Modbus device can fill the PLC role and the
  vision-output role of the same task**
- VisionOutput TCP/IP server/client (`vc::device::VisionTcpipDevice`)
- Advisory RobotKinematics checking for outgoing pick poses (`RobotKinematics::SerialRobotKinematics`)
- Hardware-free stand-ins for camera, PLC and vision output (`vc::device::VirtualCameraDevice`,
  `vc::device::VirtualPlcDevice`, `vc::device::VirtualVisionOutputDevice`) &mdash; shipped code, not
  test doubles; see `vc::device::isVirtualDevice()` and `docs/domains/virtual_devices/virtual_devices.md`

@section mp_modules Module Map

| Module | Path | Level |
|---|---|---|
| core (settings/logger/utils) | `src/core/` | 0 |
| device | `src/device/` | 1 |
| calibration | `src/calibration/` | 1 |
| matching | `src/matching/` | 1 |
| model | `src/model/` | 2 |
| runtime | `src/runtime/` | 2 |
| ui (forms + widgets) | `src/ui/` | UI |
| commissioning shell (+translations) | `components/app/` | top |
| operator runtime shell | `runtime_app/` | top |
| RobotKinematics | `components/RobotKinematics/` | component |

Lower levels must not include higher ones; `model` and `runtime` may include each other;
`device` may include `calibration`; `ui` may include every non-UI module; only the two top-level
shells may include everything, and neither may include the other. Enforced by
`tests/architecture_contract_test`.

@note `src/` is compiled exactly once, into the `ncr_shared` static library, by `src/src.pro` via
the per-module `.pri` files. No shell `.pro` lists module sources &mdash; a file registered anywhere
else is simply not built.

